\tag{frap}
\title{Further connections}

\p{[Framed orientations](frap-000A) and
[transfer and dimension](frap-000B) develop the first connections:
wreath products record positions and local transport, while abelianized
characters detect constraints when the allowed generators preserve them
\citet{Section 3.1}{marchetti2025rubik}.
Finite-index transfer organizes related calculations through coset
representatives \citet{Sections 3.1--3.3}{mayer2015artin}.
The [dimension calculation](frap-0013) explains how a local
abelianization can lose this detecting power without deciding reachability.}

\p{The following outlooks ask different questions about transport and
functions on a move group. Each needs its own construction; neither is a
prerequisite for continuing to the [layered cubes](frap-0003).}

\transclude{frap-0014}
